{{also|éloquent}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|eloquent}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|eloquens||speaking, having the faculty of speech, eloquent}}, present participle of {{m|la|eloqui||to speak out}}, from {{m|la|e||out}} + {{m|la|loqui||to speak}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈɛl.əˌkwənt/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[fluently]] [[persuasive]] and [[articulate]]
# [[effective]] in [[expressing]] [[meaning]] by [[speech]]

====Usage notes====
'''Eloquent''' expresses stronger praise than do {{m|en|articulate}} or {{m|en|well-spoken}}.

